    "turn_idx": 34,
    "turn_text": "Well, economically, we make sure that the people that we have right here in the United States are mariners are the ones taking care of our products inland and close to our shores that are not leaving off of our shores to go to other countries. Now, that is good because it keeps people working and it keeps us with trained crew in case something would break out in the world and that we would be able to know what's safe and secure. Now, then I'm going to tell you why it's important to our homeland security. Let's not be foolish and think that all of a sudden a crew that would come from, let's say, China, are some other nation that then all of a sudden we're aboard the ships that would be traveling in our ports, from port to port on the ocean, but not on that. Now inland ports, up rivers, and all of a sudden we have people that are not loyal to the United States, manning these ships when the cargo, the problem is they could sneak things in They could put us in danger. They could move explosives. They could move all kinds of things. It could make it dangerous for us. They could contaminate our waterways. They could do all kinds of damage if they don't have the loyalty to this nation. So it is a priority of mine to not only make sure I support the Jones Act, but make sure all of my colleagues understand how important it is for we this United States to make sure the Jones Act stays in place.",
